{
  "schema": "pe-solver-benchmark-cases/v1",
  "description": "Scale corpus for issue #235 (tier scale). Storage twins per game semantics with a large iteration budget and a hard memory budget (128 MiB). Hold'em runs the full 20k slot. PLO4 is capped at 5k (2.5x the committed tier baseline) because the `full` tier's cumulative commit sweep is superlinear: measured on the reference machine, plo4/full costs 53 s at 1k iterations and 140 s at 2k (total process, report phase included), so the 20k slot extrapolates to well over an hour per case. That blow-up is itself the issue-#247 finding, not a harness limit. The earlier 200k attempt collapsed to ~11x per-iteration cost late in the solve for the same reason. Issue #247 adds a second family kind: `*_budget_*` cases run under a deliberately tight RAM budget so every tier is stopped by `memory_budget` at a different iteration, which is the direct measurement of the fixed-budget criterion.",
  "defaults": {
    "players": 2,
    "iterations": 20000,
    "showdown_samples": 1,
    "br_samples": 16,
    "algorithm": "external-mccfr",
    "backend": "cpu_ref",
    "precision": "f32",
    "threads": 1,
    "seed": 20260906,
    "max_ram_mb": 128,
    "desc_limit_mb": 16,
    "report_rows": 0,
    "ranges": [
      "100%",
      "100%"
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
